../../full-run-v2.log:16:{"unit_slug":"rogue_sneak_attack","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"damage_on_hit (class_feature effect)","justification":"Sneak Attack's core payload is bonus weapon-type damage on a successful attack hit, conditioned on advantage-or-ally. ClassFeatureEffect only has grant_extra_action and heal_hp. Neither expresses conditional on-hit damage. The spell surface has DamageOnHitOperation inside ongoing_effect, but that is spell-family-only. A parallel effect atom for class features is required.","evidence":"you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack roll"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"activation_condition (class_feature conditional trigger predicate)","justification":"Sneak Attack fires only when a disjunctive condition holds: (Advantage on the roll) OR (ally within 5 ft of target, ally not Incapacitated, and no Disadvantage). No conditional trigger grammar exists anywhere in ClassFeatureMechanics. A new predicate atom is needed to express advantage-state checks and ally-proximity checks.","evidence":"if you have Advantage on the roll ... You don't need Advantage on the attack roll if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the target, the ally doesn't have the Incapacitated condition, and you don't have Disadvantage on the attack roll."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"weapon_category_filter (finesse | ranged)","justification":"Sneak Attack is restricted to attacks made with a Finesse or Ranged weapon. No weapon-category filter atom exists for class features (or at all in the surface). Without this, the surface cannot distinguish Sneak Attack from a generic damage bonus.","evidence":"the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"DamageType: weapon_type (weapon-relative source)","justification":"The extra damage type is 'the same as the weapon's type', which is a runtime-resolved value determined by the equipped weapon, not a fixed physical damage type. The current DamageType is a closed enum of 13 specific types (acid, bludgeoning, … slashing). A new variant (or a separate DamageTypeSource discriminant) is needed to express weapon-relative damage.","evidence":"The extra damage's type is the same as the weapon's type."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RestResetCadence: once_per_turn","justification":"Sneak Attack resets its once-per-use limit each turn, not on a rest. RestResetCadence has no turn variant — only short_or_long_rest, long_rest, short_rest, partial_short_full_long. Without this, the resource gate cannot be correctly modeled.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"ClassFeatureMechanics: on_hit_conditional family","justification":"Taken together, the required atoms (conditional trigger, weapon-category filter, once-per-turn gate, weapon-relative damage-on-hit with class-level scaling) compose a new structural family that is not a variant of ClassFeatureActivationMechanics. It is analogous to mastery's on_hit_trigger family but for class features with conditional predicates and level scaling. A new ClassFeatureMechanics union member is the appropriate architecture.","evidence":"Once per turn … if you have Advantage … or ally within 5 feet … Finesse or Ranged weapon … extra 1d6 … The extra damage increases as you gain Rogue levels"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_die_count' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.291}
