../../survey-results-srd.jsonl.contaminated:56:{"unit_slug":"halfling_luck","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"SpeciesTraitRecord (new UnitRecord variant)","justification":"UnitRecord = SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. No SpeciesTraitRecord exists. The tracer's traceUnit switch covers only 'spell', 'class_feature', and 'mastery'; 'species_trait' falls through to the exhaustive-never branch and throws at runtime. A new top-level record variant is required before any species-trait mechanic can be traced.","evidence":"Tracer output: 'unhandled unit kind: [object Object]' (src/interpreter/tracer.ts:90)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"reactive_trigger mechanics family","justification":"Halfling Luck is a passive always-on species trait. It has no activation cost, no use count, no rest reset, and no player-initiated trigger. The mechanic fires automatically when a specific die condition is met. SpellMechanics (activation, ongoing_effect, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger) and ClassFeatureMechanics (activation only) are all player-driven. MasteryMechanics (on_hit_trigger) is weapon-hit-only. A new 'reactive_trigger' family is needed: a passive observer that opens a window on a die result condition and grants an effect.","evidence":"When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, you can reroll the die, and you must use the new roll."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"post_roll_window","justification":"The trigger fires immediately after a d20 result is produced but before it is committed to resolution. No existing window atom covers this: reaction_window (caster's reaction to an external event), on_hit_window/on_miss_window (post-attack-resolution), post_action_window (after a creature acts on an anchor), turn_start_window/turn_end_window (turn boundaries). A new 'post_roll_window' atom is required to represent 'immediately after a die is rolled, before the result is used'.","evidence":"When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, you can reroll the die"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"die_result_condition","justification":"The trigger predicate matches a specific face (natural 1) on a specific roll scope (any D20 Test). No existing trigger or filter atom expresses 'the die shows value N'. AnchoredFilter covers creature exemption lists; ReactionTrigger covers attack-hit and named-spell targeting. A new 'die_result_condition' atom is needed with at minimum: the die scope (d20_test), the matched result (1), and optionally the roll kind.","evidence":"When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_roll_reroll","justification":"The effect is a mandatory reroll: the current die result is discarded and a fresh d20 is rolled; the new result must be used. This is distinct from (a) modify_roll_numeric (adds a fixed delta to the existing result), (b) modify_roll_advantage (grants an extra die and uses the higher/lower), and (c) any existing effect. The reroll is unconditional in direction — it does not keep the better roll — making it a distinct semantic from advantage or numeric bonus.","evidence":"you can reroll the die, and you must use the new roll"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RollKind: 'ability_check'","justification":"D20 Tests (SRD 5.2.1) encompass attack rolls, saving throws, AND ability checks. The current RollKind = 'attack_roll' | 'saving_throw' omits ability checks. Halfling Luck applies to all three, so 'ability_check' must be added to RollKind to correctly describe the trigger scope. Without it, any encoding of Luck's scope using RollKind would be incomplete.","evidence":"D20 Test — SRD 5.2.1 defines D20 Tests as attack rolls, saving throws, and ability checks."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:90\n      throw new Error(`unhandled unit kind: ${String(_exhaustive)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled unit kind: [object Object]\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:90:13)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.599}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:45:{"unit_slug":"barbarian_brutal_strike_l9","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_hit_trigger family for class_feature","justification":"Brutal Strike fires on a weapon-attack hit (conditional on Reckless Attack), not as a discrete activated feature. The only ClassFeatureMechanics family is 'activation', which demands a use-count resource and an activationCost. Brutal Strike has neither \u2014 it is an unlimited, always-available on-hit rider. A parallel 'on_hit_trigger' family for class_feature records is needed, analogous to the existing mastery 'on_hit_trigger'.","evidence":"If the chosen attack roll hits, the target takes an extra 1d10 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon or Unarmed Strike, and you can cause one Brutal Strike effect of your choice."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"optional or unlimited UseCountResource","justification":"ClassFeatureMechanicsHeader unconditionally requires a 'resource: UseCountResource'. Brutal Strike has no per-rest cap \u2014 it is available on every eligible attack. The surface needs either an optional resource field or an 'unlimited' variant of UseCountResource to represent always-on riders.","evidence":"No usage limit is stated in the source text; the feature may be triggered on every qualifying Reckless Attack hit in a turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"force_move effect in ClassFeatureEffect","justification":"Forceful Blow pushes the target 15 ft. The v4 atom 'force_move' exists in the taxonomy but is not a member of the ClassFeatureEffect union (only grant_extra_action and heal_hp are). The surface needs to admit force_move here.","evidence":"Forceful Blow: The target is pushed 15 feet straight away from you."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"modify_speed effect in ClassFeatureEffect","justification":"Hamstring Blow reduces the target's Speed by 15 ft until start of next turn. The v4 atom 'modify_speed' exists but is not a member of ClassFeatureEffect.","evidence":"Hamstring Blow: The target's Speed is reduced by 15 feet until the start of your next turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"damage (weapon-type) effect in ClassFeatureEffect","justification":"Brutal Strike adds +1d10 damage of the same type as the weapon. The v4 'damage' atom exists, but ClassFeatureEffect has no damage variant. Encoding the extra-damage rider requires admitting a damage effect here.","evidence":"the target takes an extra 1d10 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon or Unarmed Strike"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"choose_one_of effect composition","justification":"Brutal Strike lets the barbarian pick exactly one of N effect options at resolution time (Forceful Blow or Hamstring Blow). The surface has no mechanism for 'choose one from a set of effects'. This is distinct from multi-phase sequences (which are ordered) and from parallel grants.","evidence":"you can cause one Brutal Strike effect of your choice. You have the following effect options."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"prerequisite_feature link (requires Reckless Attack)","justification":"Brutal Strike is gated on using Reckless Attack this turn, creating a cross-feature dependency. The surface has no way to model 'this feature activates only when another named feature was also used this turn'.","evidence":"If you use Reckless Attack, you can forgo any Advantage on one Strength-based attack roll of your choice on your turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"self move without opportunity attacks post-hit rider","justification":"Forceful Blow also grants the attacker movement (up to half Speed) toward the target without provoking Opportunity Attacks. This is an attacker-self movement effect triggered post-hit. The v4 atoms 'move' and 'deny_opportunity_attack' exist, but there is no surface shape expressing 'caster may move X toward target after hit without OA'.","evidence":"You can then move up to half your Speed straight toward the target without provoking Opportunity Attacks."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/barbarian_brutal_strike_l9.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:169:{"unit_slug":"cleric_blessed_strikes_l7","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"choose_one_of","justification":"Blessed Strikes presents two mutually exclusive mechanical options; the player picks one permanently. No ClassFeatureMechanics family represents a 'choose one alternative' structure. The single activation family encodes exactly one effect, not a disjunction of options.","evidence":"You gain one of the following options of your choice (if you get either option from a Cleric subclass in an older book, use only the option you choose for this feature)."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"damage_on_hit_rider (ClassFeatureEffect)","justification":"Divine Strike adds extra damage on a weapon hit, once per turn. ClassFeatureEffect only contains grant_extra_action and heal_hp. The on_hit_trigger family exists only in MasteryMechanics. A class feature that grants a per-turn on-hit damage rider cannot be expressed without adding a new ClassFeatureEffect variant (or extending ClassFeatureMechanics with an on_hit_trigger family).","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice)."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"player_choice_damage_type","justification":"Divine Strike lets the player choose Necrotic or Radiant at the moment of the hit. DamageType is a single closed string; there is no 'one of [type_a, type_b] chosen at activation' variant. This is distinct from a fixed type.","evidence":"...the target to take an extra 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice)."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"add_ability_mod_to_damage","justification":"Potent Spellcasting adds the caster's Wisdom modifier (an ability score) to the damage dealt by cantrips. No v4 atom models this. modify_roll_numeric covers roll bonuses (Bless, Bane). scale_numeric_bonus covers level-scaled flat bonuses. None covers 'flat damage bonus equal to a specific ability modifier applied per-cantrip-damage-instance'.","evidence":"Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Cleric cantrip."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/cleric_blessed_strikes_l7.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:321:{"unit_slug":"druid_elemental_fury_l7","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"choose_one_of_subfeatures","justification":"The feature grants ONE of two sub-features selected at the time the druid reaches level 7. There is no wrapper shape in ClassFeatureMechanics for 'choose one of N sub-features at acquisition.' The current surface only models a single mechanics payload per record.","evidence":"You gain one of the following options of your choice."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_class_feature_family","justification":"Potent Spellcasting is a permanently-active modifier with no activation cost, no resource, and no rest reset. The only ClassFeatureMechanics family is 'activation', which requires activationCost, resource, and resetCadence \u2014 none of which apply here. A 'passive' family is needed for always-on class feature modifiers.","evidence":"Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Druid cantrip."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ability_score_damage_bonus effect","justification":"Potent Spellcasting adds the Wisdom modifier (an ability-score-derived value, not a fixed dice amount) to cantrip damage. ClassFeatureEffect supports only GrantExtraActionEffect and HealHpEffect. A new effect type is needed: a numeric damage bonus whose value is an ability modifier, scoped to a specific action class (cantrips).","evidence":"Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Druid cantrip."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_hit_trigger family for class features","justification":"Primal Strike is an on-hit damage rider once per turn, triggered by a weapon or Wild Shape Beast-form attack. This shape exists in the mastery vocabulary (OnHitTriggerMechanics) but not in ClassFeatureMechanics. No honest mapping exists without promoting a class feature to a mastery record, which misrepresents provenance.","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"choose_one_of DamageType at activation time","justification":"Primal Strike's 1d8 elemental damage type is chosen by the player at the moment of the hit, from the set {cold, fire, lightning, thunder}. DamageEffect.damageType is a single fixed DamageType with no 'choose_one_of' variant. A new surface shape is needed to express a runtime player choice among a closed set of damage types.","evidence":"you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (choose when you hit)"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"MasteryTrigger variant: weapon_or_wild_shape_beast_attack","justification":"Primal Strike fires on 'a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape.' The existing MasteryTrigger variants only cover weapon_hit and weapon_hit_melee_only. Wild Shape Beast-form natural attacks are not weapon attacks and require a new trigger category.","evidence":"when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/druid_elemental_fury_l7.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:389:{"unit_slug":"feat_boon_of_irresistible_offense","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"feat_record","justification":"No UnitRecord kind for 'feat' exists. The surface defines only spell, class_feature, and mastery records. A feat is a distinct kind with prerequisites, multiple independent benefit buckets, and no single mechanics family mapping to existing families.","evidence":"Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+) \u2014 grants Ability Score Increase, Overcome Defenses, and Overwhelming Strike as distinct, structurally independent benefits."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"crit_window","justification":"Overwhelming Strike triggers specifically on a natural 20, not on any hit. The v4 taxonomy explicitly records crit_window as a deferred single-feat pressure case for this exact feat. on_hit_window cannot distinguish a critical hit from an ordinary hit.","evidence":"When you roll a 20 on the d20 for an attack roll, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to the ability score increased by this feat."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"DiceAmount: ability_score_value","justification":"Overwhelming Strike's damage equals the character's current STR or DEX score (the one boosted by the feat) \u2014 a flat integer derived from a runtime stat. No existing DiceAmount variant (fixed, threshold_tiers, linear_per_level) can express a value that references a character ability score.","evidence":"you can deal extra damage to the target equal to the ability score increased by this feat"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"passive_benefit (bypass_resistance, always-on)","justification":"Overcome Defenses is an always-on passive \u2014 no activation, no trigger, no quota consumed. The bypass_resistance v4 atom exists, but the current surface has no passive benefit carrier. All existing ClassFeatureEffect variants are activated effects, not passive always-on modifiers.","evidence":"The Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage you deal always ignores Resistance."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/feat_boon_of_irresistible_offense.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:391:{"unit_slug":"feat_boon_of_spell_recall","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"FeatRecord","justification":"UnitRecord in types.ts has no 'feat' kind. SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord is the exhaustive union; feat_root exists in the v4 taxonomy atom inventory but has never been given a corresponding surface record type.","evidence":"Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+, Spellcasting Feature)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_spell_cast_trigger","justification":"Free Casting fires passively on every spell cast with a L1-4 slot \u2014 not an activation. The existing activation family requires an explicit activation cost. A passive trigger on spell_cast_window needs a new feat/feature family (analogous to on_hit_trigger for masteries but keyed to spell-casting events).","evidence":"Whenever you cast a spell with a level 1\u20134 spell slot, roll 1d4."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"probabilistic_roll_gate","justification":"The check is: roll 1d4, compare result to slot level (a runtime parameter). No surface type models a probabilistic check against a dynamic integer parameter. This is structurally distinct from save_gate (ability check, fixed DC) and attack_roll (vs AC). It needs a new resolution shape.","evidence":"roll 1d4. If the number you roll is the same as the slot's level, the slot isn't expended."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"refund_spell_slot","justification":"The effect on a successful check is that the spell slot is not expended \u2014 a conditional resource refund. The v4 taxonomy lists 'refund' as a procedure atom, but types.ts has no surface variant for it. The closest effect in ClassFeatureEffect is grant_extra_action or heal_hp; neither represents a slot refund.","evidence":"the slot isn't expended"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/feat_boon_of_spell_recall.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
