../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:445:{"unit_slug":"fighter_studied_attacks_l13","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_miss_trigger (class feature family)","justification":"Studied Attacks fires automatically whenever the fighter misses an attack roll \u2014 no player-initiated activation, no use-count resource, no rest reset cadence. The only existing class feature family is 'activation', which requires activationCost + resource + resetCadence. None of those fields exist for this feature. A new passive-trigger family (analogous to mastery's on_hit_trigger) is required.","evidence":"If you make an attack roll against a creature and miss, you have Advantage on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"modify_roll_advantage in ClassFeatureEffect","justification":"The feature grants Advantage on attack rolls. modify_roll_advantage exists in v4 taxonomy and is already present in MasteryEffect, but ClassFeatureEffect only contains GrantExtraActionEffect | HealHpEffect. Threading this effect type into class features is needed for Studied Attacks (and similar class features).","evidence":"you have Advantage on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/fighter_studied_attacks_l13.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:447:{"unit_slug":"fighter_superior_critical_l15","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"passive (ClassFeatureMechanics family)","justification":"Superior Critical is a permanent always-on modifier with no activation cost, no use-count resource, and no reset cadence. The existing ClassFeatureMechanics only has the 'activation' family, which requires all three. A new 'passive' family is needed for features that silently modify combat resolution without being activated.","evidence":"Your attack rolls with weapons and Unarmed Strikes can now score a Critical Hit on a roll of 18\u201320 on the d20."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_crit_threshold","justification":"The mechanic widens the d20 range that counts as a Critical Hit from 20 to 18\u201320. No existing v4 effect atom covers this. TAXONOMY_atoms_graph.md \u00a712 notes 'crit_window distinct from on_hit_window' as a deferred residue atom (single-feat pressure from Boon of Irresistible Offense). Superior Critical and Improved Critical (L3) now add two more pressure streams for this atom.","evidence":"can now score a Critical Hit on a roll of 18\u201320 on the d20"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/fighter_superior_critical_l15.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:449:{"unit_slug":"fighter_survivor_l18","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_class_feature family","justification":"ClassFeatureMechanics only has the 'activation' family, which requires activationCost + UseCountResource + resetCadence. Both Defy Death (always-on passive) and Heroic Rally (automatic turn-start trigger, no cost, no use count) cannot be honestly expressed as 'activated' features. A new family is needed for passive/automatic class feature effects.","evidence":"Defy Death: 'You have Advantage on Death Saving Throws.' (no action, no limit). Heroic Rally: 'At the start of each of your turns, you regain Hit Points...' (automatic, conditioned on state, no activation)."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"DiceAmount \u2014 flat_plus_ability_mod variant","justification":"Heroic Rally heals '5 plus your Constitution modifier'. DiceAmount only supports dice-based expressions with static flat bonuses; it has no way to express a dynamic ability modifier addend. A new variant like {kind: 'flat_plus_ability_mod', flat: number, ability: Ability} is required.","evidence":"Heroic Rally: 'you regain Hit Points equal to 5 plus your Constitution modifier'"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RollKind \u2014 death_saving_throw","justification":"Defy Death grants Advantage specifically on Death Saving Throws, which are mechanically distinct from ordinary saving throws (no ability modifier, automatic outcomes at 1/20, three-failure death). Current RollKind is 'attack_roll' | 'saving_throw' with no death-save distinction.","evidence":"Defy Death: 'You have Advantage on Death Saving Throws.'"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"conditional trigger predicate (Bloodied + HP > 0)","justification":"Heroic Rally fires only when the character is Bloodied (HP \u2264 half max) AND has at least 1 HP. No current surface type models a conditional predicate on HP state that gates an automatic effect. This is a new kind of trigger condition not present in any existing family.","evidence":"Heroic Rally: 'if you are Bloodied and have at least 1 Hit Point'"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_roll_threshold (death save 18\u201320 \u2192 20)","justification":"Defy Death's second clause widens the automatic-success threshold on Death Saving Throws from 20 to 18\u201320. v4 has no atom for 'treat rolls \u2265 N as the maximum result' on a specific roll type. This is mechanically distinct from modify_roll_advantage and from the existing crit-window pressure noted in v4 \u00a712.","evidence":"Defy Death: 'when you roll 18\u201320 on a Death Saving Throw, you gain the benefit of rolling a 20 on it.'"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/fighter_survivor_l18.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:615:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_adamantine_armor","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item UnitRecord kind","justification":"types.ts UnitRecord = SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. There is no magic_item kind. The v4 TAXONOMY has magic_item_root as a source atom but the surface has no corresponding record type. No family can be coerced to represent a magic item honestly.","evidence":"Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon \u2014 this is a magic item, not a spell, class feature, or mastery."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_persistent mechanics family","justification":"Adamantine Armor is an always-on passive modifier that fires while the item is worn, with no activation cost, no use count, and no rest reset. None of the three existing families (ongoing_effect, activation, on_hit_trigger) model a worn-item passive. A new family is needed for items whose mechanics are simply 'while wearing this, X is always true'.","evidence":"While you're wearing it, any Critical Hit against you becomes a normal hit."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"suppress_crit (or promote deferred crit_window)","justification":"The effect converts an incoming critical hit to a normal hit. No v4 atom covers this. The TAXONOMY \u00a712 explicitly defers crit_window as 'single-feat pressure, not promoted'. Adamantine Armor is a second independent pressure point (magic item stream, separate from the feat stream). The atom would need to attach to an incoming-attack resolution and downgrade the roll outcome from 'critical' to 'normal hit'.","evidence":"any Critical Hit against you becomes a normal hit"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"incoming attack_roll trigger (worn-item scope)","justification":"All existing attack_roll resolution atoms trace outgoing attacks (attacker's roll). Adamantine Armor fires on incoming attack rolls against the wearer. The surface has no trigger variant scoped to 'attack roll targeting the item bearer'. A new trigger variant or a new MasteryTrigger-equivalent for items would be needed to express 'when a critical hit is scored against the wearer'.","evidence":"any Critical Hit against you"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_adamantine_armor.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:715:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_cube_of_force","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord","justification":"UnitRecord has no 'magic_item' kind. SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord exhausts the union. A MagicItemRecord would need rarity, attunement flag, and a mechanics payload family distinct from spell/class-feature/mastery.","evidence":"Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"charge_pool_dispatcher family","justification":"The item's core mechanic is a renewable charge pool (starts 10, regains 1d6 daily at dawn) where pressing one of six faces spends N charges and casts a specific spell at a fixed DC. No existing family (ongoing_effect, activation, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, class-feature activation, on_hit_trigger) models a multi-option charge-gated spell dispatch with per-option charge cost.","evidence":"You can press one of those faces, expend the number of charges required for it, and thereby cast the spell associated with it (save DC 17), as shown in the Cube of Force Faces table."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"charge resource with dice-based daily recharge","justification":"UseCountResource only models use_count with rest-based or fixed reset. The Cube of Force uses a shared charge pool (10 charges max) that regains 1d6 charges daily at dawn \u2014 a dice-roll partial recharge on a time cadence not expressible by RestResetCadence. The v4 taxonomy has 'charge' as a resource atom but the surface types.ts has no corresponding type.","evidence":"The cube starts with 10 charges, and it regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"DcSource: fixed numeric DC","justification":"DcSource supports caster_spell_save_dc and weapon_attack_dc only. The Cube of Force specifies a fixed save DC of 17 that does not derive from the user's stats \u2014 requires a new { kind: 'fixed'; value: number } variant.","evidence":"thereby cast the spell associated with it (save DC 17)"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RestResetCadence: daily_at_dawn_dice","justification":"RestResetCadence covers short_rest, long_rest, short_or_long_rest, and partial_short_full_long. A daily recharge that yields a random dice amount (1d6) at a fixed real-time cadence (dawn) is not a rest event and cannot be expressed with the current union.","evidence":"it regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_cube_of_force.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:721:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_dancing_sword","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord","justification":"No magic_item kind exists in UnitRecord. The current union is SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. Magic items need a new top-level record type (UnitMetadata & { kind: 'magic_item'; requiresAttunement: boolean; mechanics: MagicItemMechanics }) before any encoding can proceed.","evidence":"Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"attack_proxy_family","justification":"The Dancing Sword creates an autonomous weapon proxy that flies, repositions, and attacks independently using the wielder's attack roll and ability modifier. It tracks a 4-attack budget before auto-returning. No existing mechanics family (ongoing_effect, activation, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, on_hit_trigger) can honestly represent: (a) an autonomous proxy making independent attacks, (b) a per-use countdown driving a forced lifecycle transition (return-to-hand), (c) repeatable Bonus-Action reposition+attack on subsequent turns. The v4 taxonomy has attack_proxy attachment and create_attack_proxy effect atoms, but no family wires them into a coherent subgraph.","evidence":"the weapon begins to hover, flies up to 30 feet, and attacks one creature of your choice within 5 feet of itself. The weapon uses your attack roll and adds your ability modifier to damage rolls. [...] After the hovering weapon attacks for the fourth time, it flies back to you"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"attune procedure in surface types","justification":"Attunement is a prerequisite for this item and is listed as a v4 atom ('attune') in TAXONOMY_atoms_graph.md, but there is no attunement_slot resource, no attune procedure, and no attunement_slot cap in types.ts. Any honest MagicItemRecord encoding needs attunement modeled at the surface.","evidence":"Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_dancing_sword.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:727:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_defender","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item kind. types.ts only exports SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. A MagicItemRecord family is required before any magic item can be encoded.","evidence":"Weapon (Any Melee Weapon), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_enchantment family","justification":"The +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls is a passive always-on property of the weapon, not an activated effect. No existing mechanics family (activation, ongoing_effect, on_hit_trigger) models a passive item enchantment that applies without any activation cost.","evidence":"You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"attunement procedure","justification":"The item requires attunement. The v4 taxonomy has an 'attune' procedure atom and 'attunement_slot' resource atom, but neither is represented in types.ts. Encoding attunement requires new surface types for the attune procedure and attunement_slot resource.","evidence":"Legendary (Requires Attunement)"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"variable_bonus_split operation","justification":"The transfer mechanic lets the wielder dynamically reallocate a shared +N bonus between two targets (attack/damage rolls vs AC). The split is a free integer choice per first-attack-of-turn (e.g., +1 attack/+2 AC, or +0 attack/+3 AC). Current surface types model fixed-delta effects (modify_roll_numeric, modify_ac). There is no surface type for a shared-pool bonus that can be partitioned at runtime across two distinct effect targets.","evidence":"you can transfer some or all of the weapon's bonus to your Armor Class. For example, you could reduce the bonus to your attack rolls and damage rolls to +1 and gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_defender.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:757:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_elven_chain","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item UnitRecord kind","justification":"No magic_item kind exists in UnitRecord. types.ts only defines SpellRecord, ClassFeatureRecord, and MasteryRecord. The v4 taxonomy lists magic_item_root as a source atom and attune as a procedure atom, but the schema layer never wired them into a UnitRecord variant. Every magic item hits this wall before any atom-level question arises.","evidence":"Armor (Chain Mail or Chain Shirt), Rare \u2014 the item category itself has no surface home"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_property mechanics family","justification":"Elven Chain's +1 AC and proficiency grant are always-on while worn \u2014 no activation cost, no use-count, no spell slot. The existing families (activation for class features, on_hit_trigger for masteries, spell families for spells) all require an action or trigger. Magic items with static worn effects need a passive_property or worn_property family that emits a persist-like lifecycle rooted on the item.","evidence":"You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class while you wear this armor."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"grant_proficiency as a surface effect type","justification":"grant_proficiency exists in v4 taxonomy (\u00a79 Effect Atoms) but is not exposed in types.ts as any Effect or ClassFeatureEffect variant. Elven Chain's training override \u2014 'considered trained with this armor even if you lack training' \u2014 requires it. This would be a surface_widening relative to the class-feature effect union, but it only becomes relevant once MagicItemRecord exists.","evidence":"You are considered trained with this armor even if you lack training with Medium or Heavy armor."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"modify_ac as a standalone passive effect (not just ReactionEffect)","justification":"modify_ac appears in types.ts only as a ReactionEffect (Shield-style: fires once, during a triggered reaction window). Elven Chain's +1 AC is a persistent addend while worn \u2014 not reaction-gated. A passive modify_ac variant (or a worn_property effect shape) is needed to represent it honestly.","evidence":"You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class while you wear this armor."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_elven_chain.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:765:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_eyes_of_minute_seeing","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item kind","justification":"UnitRecord = SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord \u2014 no MagicItemRecord exists. The tracer's traceUnit switch has no 'magic_item' branch and would throw. The v4 taxonomy lists magic_item_root as a source atom, but the surface type system has no corresponding record shape.","evidence":"Wondrous Item, Uncommon \u2014 the unit kind is magic_item, which has no entry in UnitRecord"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_equip mechanics family","justification":"Eyes of Minute Seeing has no activation, no casting time, no use count, no reset cadence. Its effects are always-on while the item is worn. No existing mechanics family (activation, ongoing_effect, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, on_hit_trigger) models a passive equip effect. A new family (e.g. passive_equip or equip_effect) is needed for magic items whose mechanics are unconditionally active while worn.","evidence":"While wearing them, your vision improves significantly \u2014 no action, no resource, no trigger"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_sense (surface exposure)","justification":"grant_sense exists in the v4 taxonomy (\u00a79 Effect Atoms) but is not defined in types.ts as a surface type. The Darkvision-within-1-foot effect maps directly to grant_sense, but the surface type system has no GrantSenseEffect variant. The tracer would have nowhere to route it.","evidence":"granting you Darkvision within that range"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ability_check in RollKind","justification":"RollKind = 'attack_roll' | 'saving_throw'. The Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks effect needs a third variant 'ability_check' (or a typed sub-variant like 'intelligence_check'). The existing modify_roll_advantage shape requires a RollKind[] for its 'on' field, and ability checks are not covered.","evidence":"Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to examine something within that range"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_eyes_of_minute_seeing.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:771:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_figurine_of_wondrous_power","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item family","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item kind. The taxonomy lists magic_item_root as a source atom but types.ts has no MagicItemRecord, no MagicItemMechanics, and no mechanics family to house it. Every existing family (activation, ongoing_effect, on_hit_trigger, anchored_trigger, triggered_reaction) is incompatible with item semantics.","evidence":"If you take a Magic action to throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, the figurine becomes a living creature... The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form... its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"day_cooldown variant of RestResetCadence (or new ItemRechargeKind)","justification":"Figurine recharge is measured in days (2, 5, 7, 15, 30 days) \u2014 not short/long rest. RestResetCadence has no variant for calendar-time recharge. A new closed type (e.g. DayCooldown { days: number }) is needed.","evidence":"Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed. / Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"charge_pool with day-recharge (Goat of Traveling pattern)","justification":"Goat of Traveling uses a 24-charge pool where each hour of use costs 1 charge and the pool recharges after 7 days when empty. This is neither use_count (fixed cap + rest reset) nor spell_slot. Needs a charge resource with duration-based consumption and day-count recharge.","evidence":"It has 24 charges, and each hour or portion thereof it spends in goat form costs 1 charge. When it runs out of charges, it reverts to a figurine and can't be used again until 7 days have passed, when it regains all expended charges."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"multi-variant item (one item slug, several named sub-configurations)","justification":"The Figurine of Wondrous Power is a single item category with nine distinct named variants (Bronze Griffon, Ebony Fly, Golden Lions, Ivory Goats \u00d7 3, Marble Elephant, Obsidian Steed, Onyx Dog, Serpentine Owl, Silver Raven). No surface type models this one-to-many item/variant relationship.","evidence":"Bronze Griffon (Rare)... Ebony Fly (Rare)... Golden Lions (Rare)... Ivory Goats (Rare)... Obsidian Steed (Very Rare)... Onyx Dog (Rare)... Serpentine Owl (Rare)... Silver Raven (Uncommon)."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"create_companion mechanics subgraph","justification":"The core effect is summoning a named creature that acts as a friendly companion with initiative placement, obeys commands, and reverts on 0 HP or dismissal. The v4 atom create_companion exists but there is no surface mechanics shape that expresses: throw-to-point activation, creature-kind binding, duration-to-revert lifecycle, or companion command semantics.","evidence":"The creature is Friendly to you and your allies. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"probabilistic_override (Obsidian Steed 10% disobedience)","justification":"The Obsidian Steed has a 10% per-use chance to ignore all commands including revert. This is not representable by any existing resolution atom (attack_roll, save_gate, ability_check). It requires a probability-weighted override that bypasses the normal command chain.","evidence":"The figurine has a 10 percent chance each time you use it to ignore your orders, including a command to revert to figurine form."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_figurine_of_wondrous_power.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:785:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_giant_slayer","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item kind in UnitRecord","justification":"UnitRecord has no 'magic_item' kind. types.ts only defines SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. The TAXONOMY lists magic_item_root as a v4 source atom but the surface has never been extended to include it. All magic items are blocked at this level.","evidence":"Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare \u2014 the item is a magic item, a category absent from UnitRecord"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"passive_weapon_bonus family (always-on +N to attack and damage rolls)","justification":"The +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls is always-on while wielding; no existing family (activation, on_hit_trigger, ongoing_effect) models a passive item property that requires no activation, no quota, and no concentration. A new family is needed.","evidence":"You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"creature_type_filter on on-hit trigger (Giant-only rider)","justification":"MasteryTrigger only gates on weapon_hit / weapon_hit_melee_only with no creature-type predicate. Giant Slayer's rider fires only against creatures of type Giant. Encoding this without a filter would dishonestly apply the rider to all weapon hits.","evidence":"When you hit a Giant with this weapon, the Giant takes an extra 2d6 damage..."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_damage_type as a DamageType variant or special alias","justification":"DamageType is a closed enum of specific damage types (slashing, piercing, etc.). Giant Slayer deals 'damage of the weapon's type', which is resolved at runtime from the weapon. There is no 'weapon_damage_type' or 'inherited' variant in DamageType.","evidence":"the Giant takes an extra 2d6 damage of the weapon's type"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_giant_slayer.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:787:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_glamoured_studded_leather","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item kind","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item kind. SpellRecord, ClassFeatureRecord, and MasteryRecord all require domain-specific header fields (spell level/school, className/acquiredAtLevel, on_hit_trigger family) that are inapplicable to a magic item. A MagicItemRecord needs: id, name, provenance, description, item category (armor, weapon, wondrous, etc.), rarity, attunement requirement, and a MagicItemMechanics union.","evidence":"Armor (Studded Leather Armor), Rare \u2014 neither a spell, class feature, nor mastery; has rarity and item-type metadata that no existing record type carries."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_always_on family for MagicItemMechanics","justification":"The +1 AC bonus is always active while wearing \u2014 no activation cost, no resource consumed, no trigger. All current families (activation, ongoing_effect, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, on_hit_trigger) require an activation event or spell-slot cost. A passive_always_on family would model 'while worn/attuned, effect X is permanently active' and emit a modify_ac (or modify_roll_numeric) atom attached to self with no procedure node.","evidence":"While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"activated_property family for MagicItemMechanics","justification":"The glamour property is a Bonus Action activation that applies alter_item_kind effect. It needs: bonus_action_quota consumed, alter_item_kind effect (v4 atom exists), and a novel expiry model ('until you use this property again or doff the armor'). No existing family covers item-property activations with unlimited-use (no use_count) bonus-action costs.","evidence":"You can also take a Bonus Action to cause the armor to assume the appearance of a normal set of clothing or some other kind of armor."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"item_doffed expiry variant for lifecycle atoms","justification":"The glamour lasts 'until you use this property again or doff the armor.' Neither turn_start_window, turn_end_window, rest_window, nor expire covers an equip/doff event. An item_doffed lifecycle event (or equip_window atom) is needed to represent 'ends when the item is removed'.","evidence":"The illusory appearance lasts until you use this property again or doff the armor."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_glamoured_studded_leather.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:801:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_hat_of_disguise","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord","justification":"UnitRecord has no 'magic_item' kind. The surface type union only contains SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. A MagicItemRecord variant (with id, name, provenance, description, and a MagicItemMechanics discriminant) is required before any magic item can be encoded.","evidence":"Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemMechanics / spell_grant family","justification":"The hat's mechanic is: while attuned and wearing the item, you may cast a named spell (Disguise Self) at will with no spell slot consumed. No existing family (ongoing_effect, activation, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, class-feature activation, on_hit_trigger) can honestly represent 'item grants at-will named-spell casting'. A new family \u2014 tentatively spell_grant \u2014 is needed, carrying: the granted spellId, the activation cost (action), the resource (no slot consumed, item-charges or unlimited), and the duration/expiry of the granted spell.","evidence":"While wearing this hat, you can cast the Disguise Self spell."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Duration: while_worn (item-conditioned expiry)","justification":"The spell ends when the hat is removed. Disguise Self's normal duration is 1 hour (timed), but here the expiry is additionally conditioned on the item being worn. None of the existing Duration variants (instantaneous, concentration, timed) express 'ends if item removed'. A new Duration kind \u2014 e.g. { kind: 'while_worn' } \u2014 or a composable expiry modifier is required.","evidence":"The spell ends if the hat is removed."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"AttunementRequirement on MagicItemRecord","justification":"The item requires attunement. The attune procedure atom exists in v4, but the surface type has no field or subtype to record whether a magic item requires attunement and which attunement_slot it binds. MagicItemRecord needs an attunement field.","evidence":"Requires Attunement"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_hat_of_disguise.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:837:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_lantern_of_revealing","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"magic_item_record","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item kind. MagicItemRecord is absent from the type system entirely \u2014 SpellRecord, ClassFeatureRecord, and MasteryRecord are the only options, none of which accept item-specific metadata (rarity, attunement, item type).","evidence":"Lantern of Revealing is a 'Wondrous Item, Uncommon' \u2014 a magic item, not a spell, class feature, or mastery."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_aura_family","justification":"The lantern's core mechanic is a persistent spatial effect (light emission + invisibility reveal) that is always-on while the item is lit. No existing mechanics family covers passive item properties \u2014 all families require an activation event (activate, respond, store, on_hit_trigger). A passive_aura or item_property family is needed for always-on conditional effects.","evidence":"While lit, this hooded lantern burns for 6 hours on 1 pint of oil, shedding Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"reveal_invisible","justification":"Making invisible creatures and objects perceptible within the lantern's Bright Light is mechanically distinct from grant_sense (which grants a sense capability to a creature) and from any existing effect atom. The effect suppresses the concealment benefit of invisibility for all observers, not for a specific creature gaining a sense.","evidence":"Invisible creatures and objects are visible as long as they are in the lantern's Bright Light."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"utilize_action_cost","justification":"The hood-lowering uses a Utilize action. ClassFeatureActivationCost only has 'free' and 'bonus_action'; StandardActionKind includes 'utilize' but no activation cost variant maps to it. A magic item mechanics layer would need utilize_action as an activation cost option.","evidence":"You can take a Utilize action to lower the hood, reducing the lantern's light to Dim Light in a 5-foot radius."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_lantern_of_revealing.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:843:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_mace_of_smiting","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord","justification":"No magic_item kind exists in UnitRecord. types.ts defines SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord only. The taxonomy lists magic_item_root as a source atom but the surface type system has no corresponding record type or mechanics family.","evidence":"Mace of Smiting \u2014 Weapon (Mace), Rare"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"crit_window","justification":"The extra damage fires specifically on a critical hit (rolling a natural 20). The existing on_hit_window covers any hit; crit_window is mechanically distinct. The taxonomy already notes this as a known weak spot (single-feat pressure from Boon of Irresistible Offense). Mace of Smiting is a second independent pressure case.","evidence":"When you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 7 Bludgeoning damage"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"creature_type_filter","justification":"Both the bonus escalation (+1 \u2192 +3) and the crit damage escalation (7 \u2192 14) are conditioned on whether the target is a Construct. No creature-type predicate exists on any Attachment, DcSource, DiceAmount, or effect variant. This is a new conditional axis not present anywhere in v4.","evidence":"The bonus increases to +3 when you use the weapon to attack a Construct. [...] or 14 Bludgeoning damage if it's a Construct."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"instant_kill_at_hp_threshold","justification":"If a Construct has 25 HP or fewer after taking the crit damage, it is destroyed. This is a deterministic instant-kill conditioned on post-damage remaining HP. v4 has no effect atom for HP-threshold destruction; apply_condition covers conditions, not creature destruction.","evidence":"If a Construct has 25 Hit Points or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_weapon_bonus family","justification":"The +1 to attack and damage rolls is a passive always-on property of the weapon itself, active every time the weapon is used \u2014 not an activation, not a spell, not a mastery on-hit rider. There is no passive-property family for magic items in the current surface. The closest existing shape (ongoing_effect) requires a spell header and caster action; modify_roll_numeric requires a procedure that grants it.","evidence":"You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_mace_of_smiting.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:885:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_periapt_of_proof_against_poison","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + passive_while_attuned family","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item variant. The item's mechanic is a passive always-on effect while worn and attuned \u2014 no activation, no cost, no reset. No existing mechanics family (activation, ongoing_effect, on_hit_trigger, etc.) honestly represents this shape. A new top-level record kind and a new mechanics family are both required.","evidence":"While you wear it, you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition and Poison damage."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_immunity","justification":"v4 has grant_resistance (halved damage) but not grant_immunity (no damage/effect). These are mechanically distinct in SRD 5.2.1 \u2014 immunity fully negates while resistance halves. A separate atom is required to avoid a dishonest encoding that collapses the two.","evidence":"you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition and Poison damage"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_condition_immunity","justification":"v4 has apply_condition and remove_condition but no atom for granting permanent immunity to a condition. Condition immunity is mechanically distinct from resistance (which applies only to damage) and from remove_condition (which is a one-time effect).","evidence":"you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"attunement requirement on item record","justification":"The item requires attunement. v4 has attunement_slot as a resource atom and attune as a procedure atom, but the surface has no field on a hypothetical MagicItemRecord to express requires_attunement as a gate. This is a structural surface gap, not just a missing atom.","evidence":"Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_periapt_of_proof_against_poison.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1007:{"unit_slug":"monk_open_hand_technique_l3","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"ClassFeatureOnHitTriggerMechanics (family: on_hit_trigger)","justification":"Open Hand Technique fires on a hit from a specific action source (Flurry of Blows), not from a free activation. ClassFeatureMechanics has only the 'activation' family, which presupposes an activationCost + use_count resource. This unit needs an on-hit rider family for ClassFeatureRecord, parallel to MasteryMechanics['on_hit_trigger'] but binding to a named action source rather than a weapon-type filter.","evidence":"Whenever you hit a creature with an attack granted by your Flurry of Blows, you can impose one of the following effects on that target."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"MasteryTrigger (or new ClassFeatureTrigger) :: action_source_hit","justification":"The trigger is constrained to 'attacks granted by Flurry of Blows'. Existing MasteryTrigger variants (weapon_hit, weapon_hit_melee_only) filter by weapon kind, not by action source. A new variant carrying an action source identifier (e.g. 'flurry_of_blows') is needed.","evidence":"...an attack granted by your Flurry of Blows..."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ChooseEffect (player chooses one-of N effects)","justification":"The feature presents a menu of three independent effects and the player picks one per trigger. Neither ClassFeatureEffect nor MasteryEffect has a 'choose_from' composition. The v4 taxonomy lists 'choose' as a procedure atom but there is no surface type that wraps a ReadonlyArray of candidate effects under a player-choice gate.","evidence":"...you can impose one of the following effects on that target. Addle. / Push. / Topple."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"SaveGateRiderResult :: deny_opportunity_attack","justification":"Addle grants an automatic on-hit effect (no save) that denies Opportunity Attacks until turn start. deny_opportunity_attack is a v4 effect atom but is absent from SaveGateRiderResult and ClassFeatureEffect. Additionally, Addle has no save gate at all \u2014 it is unconditional on hit \u2014 so even extending SaveGateRiderResult is insufficient; a separate 'auto_on_hit' effect slot is needed.","evidence":"Addle. The target can't make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"SaveGateRiderResult :: force_move","justification":"Push force-moves the target up to 15 feet on a failed STR save. force_move is a v4 atom but is absent from SaveGateRiderResult (which only has apply_condition and none) and from ClassFeatureEffect.","evidence":"Push. The target must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 15 feet away from you."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/monk_open_hand_technique_l3.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1155:{"unit_slug":"ranger_hunters_prey_l3","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_on_hit_rider (class feature family)","justification":"Colossus Slayer is a passive weapon-hit rider on the class feature record. The only class feature family is 'activation', which requires an activationCost + use_count resource + resetCadence + effect. Colossus Slayer has none of these \u2014 it is always-on (while chosen) and fires passively on each qualifying weapon hit. Forcing it into 'activation' would misrepresent the mechanic entirely.","evidence":"When you hit a creature with a weapon, the weapon deals an extra 1d8 damage to the target if it's missing any of its Hit Points. You can deal this extra damage only once per turn."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_on_attack_rider (class feature family)","justification":"Horde Breaker fires when the ranger *makes* a weapon attack (before resolution, not on hit). There is no 'on_attack_window' atom \u2014 only 'on_hit_window'. The trigger is pre-resolution, granting a second optional weapon attack against a different creature. This is not 'activation' and not 'on_hit_trigger'.","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you make an attack with a weapon, you can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target, that is within the weapon's range, and that you haven't attacked this turn."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"choose_one_of_N_options (top-level class feature choice structure)","justification":"Hunter's Prey is not a single feature \u2014 it is a container that grants one of two sub-options, replaceable on Short or Long Rest. There is no vocabulary in UnitRecord, ClassFeatureRecord, or ClassFeatureMechanics for 'choose one of these variants, swappable on rest'. Both individual options and the choice structure itself require new surface support.","evidence":"You gain one of the following feature options of your choice. Whenever you finish a Short or Long Rest, you can replace the chosen option with the other one."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"hp_below_max_predicate (conditional filter on damage_on_hit)","justification":"Colossus Slayer's +1d8 only applies if the target is currently missing HP. This is a runtime predicate on the creature's HP state that gates whether the rider fires. No existing atom or filter variant captures this check. The closest existing concept is a save gate, but this is a passive HP-state check, not a save.","evidence":"the weapon deals an extra 1d8 damage to the target if it's missing any of its Hit Points"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"on_attack_window","justification":"Horde Breaker's trigger is 'when you make an attack with a weapon' \u2014 before attack roll resolution. The v4 atom inventory has on_hit_window and on_miss_window (post-resolution) but no pre-resolution attack window. This is a distinct timing point needed for Horde Breaker and analogous features.","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you make an attack with a weapon, you can make another attack..."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/ranger_hunters_prey_l3.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1201:{"unit_slug":"rogue_cunning_strike_l5","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_sneak_attack_hit_trigger (class feature family)","justification":"Cunning Strike fires when Sneak Attack damage is dealt \u2014 it is not a standalone activation. No existing ClassFeatureMechanics family has an on-hit trigger shape. The mastery 'on_hit_trigger' family covers weapon hits but is not usable for class features (different UnitRecord kind). A parallel family for class features is required.","evidence":"When you deal Sneak Attack damage, you can add one of the following Cunning Strike effects."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"dice_cost resource (forgo Sneak Attack damage dice)","justification":"Each Cunning Strike effect costs 1d6 of Sneak Attack damage \u2014 the rogue removes those dice before rolling. This 'forgo N damage dice' pattern does not exist in any current resource atom. It is not use_count, action_quota, bonus_action_quota, or spell_slot.","evidence":"Each effect has a die cost, which is the number of Sneak Attack damage dice you must forgo to add the effect. You remove the die before rolling."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"menu_of_effects (choose one at use-time)","justification":"Cunning Strike exposes a set of effects the rogue selects from each time the trigger fires. The current surface has no construct for 'pick one of N effects when activating'. ClassFeatureActivationMechanics has a single effect field; mastery effects are also singular.","evidence":"you can add one of the following Cunning Strike effects"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Condition: poisoned","justification":"The Poison effect applies the Poisoned condition. The current Condition type only contains 'prone'. Poisoned must be added to the Condition union.","evidence":"the target has the Poisoned condition for 1 minute"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"repeat_save (save at end of each of target's turns)","justification":"The Poison effect includes a repeating save: 'At the end of each of its turns, the Poisoned target repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success.' This is a distinct resolution shape from the single save_gate atom \u2014 it is a persist+repeat_save lifecycle. Nothing in the current surface covers this.","evidence":"At the end of each of its turns, the Poisoned target repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"size_constraint on save_gate (Large or smaller)","justification":"The Trip effect only applies to targets that are Large or smaller. No current surface type allows a target-size predicate to gate whether the effect fires.","evidence":"If the target is Large or smaller, it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"move effect for ClassFeatureEffect (Withdraw: half speed, no OA)","justification":"The Withdraw effect grants movement (up to half Speed) without provoking Opportunity Attacks. Neither 'move' nor 'deny_opportunity_attack' (both v4 atoms) exist in the ClassFeatureEffect union. They would need to be added.","evidence":"Immediately after the attack, you move up to half your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/rogue_cunning_strike_l5.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1225:{"unit_slug":"rogue_sneak_attack","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"class_feature.on_hit_trigger","justification":"Sneak Attack is a passive class feature whose core mechanic is an on-hit rider, but class_feature only supports the activation family.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack roll"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"class_feature.on_hit_trigger.qualifying_predicates","justification":"The surface needs to express Sneak Attack's eligibility gates: finesse or ranged weapon, advantage OR nearby non-incapacitated ally, and no disadvantage.","evidence":"if you have Advantage on the roll and the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon. You don't need Advantage ... if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the target, the ally doesn't have the Incapacitated condition, and you don't have Disadvantage"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"damage_type_from_weapon_hit","justification":"Existing damage surfaces require a fixed damage type, but Sneak Attack inherits the damage type from the qualifying weapon hit.","evidence":"The extra damage's type is the same as the weapon's type."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/rogue_sneak_attack.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1227:{"unit_slug":"rogue_sneak_attack_l1","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_hit_trigger family for ClassFeatureMechanics","justification":"Sneak Attack is a passive damage rider on weapon attack rolls, not an activated feature. ClassFeatureMechanics only has the 'activation' family. A new family analogous to MasteryMechanics.OnHitTriggerMechanics is needed for class features that are passive on-hit riders.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack roll"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"damage_on_hit ClassFeatureEffect variant","justification":"ClassFeatureEffect is limited to grant_extra_action and heal_hp. Sneak Attack needs a damage-rider effect type with a scaling DiceAmount.","evidence":"deal an extra 1d6 damage ... The extra damage increases as you gain Rogue levels"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_type variable DamageType","justification":"DamageType is a closed 13-value enum. Sneak Attack's damage type inherits from the weapon, which is not representable as any fixed literal. A variant such as 'weapon_damage_type' or a tagged union that marks the type as derived from the weapon is needed.","evidence":"The extra damage's type is the same as the weapon's type."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"disjunctive precondition gate for on-hit triggers","justification":"Sneak Attack fires only if Advantage is held OR (ally within 5 ft AND no Disadvantage). No existing surface type models disjunctive/conjunctive preconditions on attack-roll riders. The mastery trigger vocabulary (weapon_hit / weapon_hit_melee_only) is unconditional.","evidence":"if you have Advantage on the roll ... You don't need Advantage on the attack roll if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the target, the ally doesn't have the Incapacitated condition, and you don't have Disadvantage on the attack roll."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_property filter (Finesse or Ranged)","justification":"Sneak Attack is restricted to Finesse or Ranged weapons. No existing trigger or attachment type models a weapon-property filter.","evidence":"the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/rogue_sneak_attack_l1.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1337:{"unit_slug":"species_dragonborn_draconic_ancestry","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"species_trait kind + SpeciesTraitRecord","justification":"UnitRecord in types.ts has no species_trait variant. The tracer's traceUnit switch handles only spell, class_feature, and mastery \u2014 there is no code path for a species trait record at all.","evidence":"As a Dragonborn, you have these special traits. ***Draconic Ancestry.*** Your lineage stems from a dragon progenitor. Choose the kind of dragon from the Draconic Ancestors table."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"lineage_choice mechanics family","justification":"Draconic Ancestry is a passive character-creation parameter choice: the player selects a dragon type which sets a damage type used by Breath Weapon and Damage Resistance. This pattern \u2014 a deferred-parameter selection with no activation cost, no use-count, no attack roll, and no save \u2014 fits no existing mechanics family (activation, ongoing_effect, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, on_hit_trigger). A new family is needed to represent 'choose-at-creation parameter that parameterizes other traits'.","evidence":"Choose the kind of dragon from the Draconic Ancestors table. Your choice affects your Breath Weapon and Damage Resistance traits as well as your appearance."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/species_dragonborn_draconic_ancestry.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1361:{"unit_slug":"species_gnome_gnomish_cunning","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"SpeciesTraitRecord + passive_modifier family","justification":"UnitRecord has no species_trait kind. The trait is passive and always-on \u2014 no activation cost, no use-count resource, no reset cadence. No existing family (activation, on_hit_trigger, ongoing_effect, etc.) can represent this honestly.","evidence":"You have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"modify_roll_advantage as a passive species-trait effect","justification":"The v4 atom modify_roll_advantage exists but is only wired into MasteryEffect (on-hit riders). A passive_modifier family for species traits would need a SpeciesTraitEffect variant that expresses unconditional advantage on a closed set of saving-throw ability scores, attached to self with no window or resolution intermediary.","evidence":"You have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/species_gnome_gnomish_cunning.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
../../survey-results-srd.jsonl:1635:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_rod_of_lordly_might","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"magic_item_mode_switch","justification":"The item has six mutually exclusive persistent button states, each entered by a Bonus Action and lasting until another button is pressed or toggled off. The current MagicItemRecord can carry only one mechanics family and has no way to represent item-local mode state with replacement semantics across passive and utility forms.","evidence":"\"You can press one of the following buttons as a Bonus Action; a button's effect lasts until you push a different button or until you push the same button again, which causes the rod to revert to its normal form.\""},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"magic_item_composite_mechanics","justification":"The rod combines always-on weapon bonuses, persistent alternate forms, on-hit optional riders with dawn resets, and a separate Magic action fear ability. The current magic-item surface forces one top-level mechanics family (`passive` or `activation`) and cannot honestly encode a multi-property item with independent triggers and resources.","evidence":"\"It has three other properties as well, detailed below.\""},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"MagicItemMechanics.on_hit_trigger","justification":"Drain Life and Paralyze are optional riders that trigger when the wielder hits with a melee attack using the rod. `on_hit_trigger` exists only for mastery, not for magic items, so these cannot be represented without widening the magic-item mechanics union or introducing composition.","evidence":"\"When you hit a creature with a melee attack using the rod, you can force the target to make a DC 17 Constitution saving throw.\""}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no conte