../../results-srd/magic_item_elven_chain/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_elven_chain","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item UnitRecord kind","justification":"No magic_item kind exists in UnitRecord. types.ts only defines SpellRecord, ClassFeatureRecord, and MasteryRecord. The v4 taxonomy lists magic_item_root as a source atom and attune as a procedure atom, but the schema layer never wired them into a UnitRecord variant. Every magic item hits this wall before any atom-level question arises.","evidence":"Armor (Chain Mail or Chain Shirt), Rare — the item category itself has no surface home"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_property mechanics family","justification":"Elven Chain's +1 AC and proficiency grant are always-on while worn — no activation cost, no use-count, no spell slot. The existing families (activation for class features, on_hit_trigger for masteries, spell families for spells) all require an action or trigger. Magic items with static worn effects need a passive_property or worn_property family that emits a persist-like lifecycle rooted on the item.","evidence":"You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class while you wear this armor."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"grant_proficiency as a surface effect type","justification":"grant_proficiency exists in v4 taxonomy (§9 Effect Atoms) but is not exposed in types.ts as any Effect or ClassFeatureEffect variant. Elven Chain's training override — 'considered trained with this armor even if you lack training' — requires it. This would be a surface_widening relative to the class-feature effect union, but it only becomes relevant once MagicItemRecord exists.","evidence":"You are considered trained with this armor even if you lack training with Medium or Heavy armor."