../../results-srd/druid_elemental_fury_l7/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"druid_elemental_fury_l7","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"choose_one_of_subfeatures","justification":"The feature grants ONE of two sub-features selected at the time the druid reaches level 7. There is no wrapper shape in ClassFeatureMechanics for 'choose one of N sub-features at acquisition.' The current surface only models a single mechanics payload per record.","evidence":"You gain one of the following options of your choice."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_class_feature_family","justification":"Potent Spellcasting is a permanently-active modifier with no activation cost, no resource, and no rest reset. The only ClassFeatureMechanics family is 'activation', which requires activationCost, resource, and resetCadence — none of which apply here. A 'passive' family is needed for always-on class feature modifiers.","evidence":"Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Druid cantrip."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ability_score_damage_bonus effect","justification":"Potent Spellcasting adds the Wisdom modifier (an ability-score-derived value, not a fixed dice amount) to cantrip damage. ClassFeatureEffect supports only GrantExtraActionEffect and HealHpEffect. A new effect type is needed: a numeric damage bonus whose value is an ability modifier, scoped to a specific action class (cantrips).","evidence":"Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Druid cantrip."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_hit_trigger family for class features","justification":"Primal Strike is an on-hit damage rider once per turn, triggered by a weapon or Wild Shape Beast-form attack. This shape exists in the mastery vocabulary (OnHitTriggerMechanics) but not in ClassFeatureMechanics. No honest mapping exists without promoting a class feature to a mastery record, which misrepresents provenance.","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"choose_one_of DamageType at activation time","justification":"Primal Strike's 1d8 elemental damage type is chosen by the player at the moment of the hit, from the set {cold, fire, lightning, thunder}. DamageEffect.damageType is a single fixed DamageType with no 'choose_one_of' variant. A new surface shape is needed to express a runtime player choice among a closed set of damage types.","evidence":"you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (choose when you hit)"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"MasteryTrigger variant: weapon_or_wild_shape_beast_attack","justification":"Primal Strike fires on 'a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape.' The existing MasteryTrigger variants only cover weapon_hit and weapon_hit_melee_only. Wild Shape Beast-form natural attacks are not weapon attacks and require a new trigger category.","evidence":"when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/druid_elemental_fury_l7.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
