../../results-srd/rogue_cunning_strike_l5/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"rogue_cunning_strike_l5","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"on_sneak_attack_hit_trigger (class feature family)","justification":"Cunning Strike fires when Sneak Attack damage is dealt — it is not a standalone activation. No existing ClassFeatureMechanics family has an on-hit trigger shape. The mastery 'on_hit_trigger' family covers weapon hits but is not usable for class features (different UnitRecord kind). A parallel family for class features is required.","evidence":"When you deal Sneak Attack damage, you can add one of the following Cunning Strike effects."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"dice_cost resource (forgo Sneak Attack damage dice)","justification":"Each Cunning Strike effect costs 1d6 of Sneak Attack damage — the rogue removes those dice before rolling. This 'forgo N damage dice' pattern does not exist in any current resource atom. It is not use_count, action_quota, bonus_action_quota, or spell_slot.","evidence":"Each effect has a die cost, which is the number of Sneak Attack damage dice you must forgo to add the effect. You remove the die before rolling."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"menu_of_effects (choose one at use-time)","justification":"Cunning Strike exposes a set of effects the rogue selects from each time the trigger fires. The current surface has no construct for 'pick one of N effects when activating'. ClassFeatureActivationMechanics has a single effect field; mastery effects are also singular.","evidence":"you can add one of the following Cunning Strike effects"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Condition: poisoned","justification":"The Poison effect applies the Poisoned condition. The current Condition type only contains 'prone'. Poisoned must be added to the Condition union.","evidence":"the target has the Poisoned condition for 1 minute"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"repeat_save (save at end of each of target's turns)","justification":"The Poison effect includes a repeating save: 'At the end of each of its turns, the Poisoned target repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success.' This is a distinct resolution shape from the single save_gate atom — it is a persist+repeat_save lifecycle. Nothing in the current surface covers this.","evidence":"At the end of each of its turns, the Poisoned target repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"size_constraint on save_gate (Large or smaller)","justification":"The Trip effect only applies to targets that are Large or smaller. No current surface type allows a target-size predicate to gate whether the effect fires.","evidence":"If the target is Large or smaller, it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"move effect for ClassFeatureEffect (Withdraw: half speed, no OA)","justification":"The Withdraw effect grants movement (up to half Speed) without provoking Opportunity Attacks. Neither 'move' nor 'deny_opportunity_attack' (both v4 atoms) exist in the ClassFeatureEffect union. They would need to be added.","evidence":"Immediately after the attack, you move up to half your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/rogue_cunning_strike_l5.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
