../../results-srd/magic_item_figurine_of_wondrous_power/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_figurine_of_wondrous_power","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + magic_item family","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item kind. The taxonomy lists magic_item_root as a source atom but types.ts has no MagicItemRecord, no MagicItemMechanics, and no mechanics family to house it. Every existing family (activation, ongoing_effect, on_hit_trigger, anchored_trigger, triggered_reaction) is incompatible with item semantics.","evidence":"If you take a Magic action to throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, the figurine becomes a living creature... The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form... its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"day_cooldown variant of RestResetCadence (or new ItemRechargeKind)","justification":"Figurine recharge is measured in days (2, 5, 7, 15, 30 days) — not short/long rest. RestResetCadence has no variant for calendar-time recharge. A new closed type (e.g. DayCooldown { days: number }) is needed.","evidence":"Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed. / Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"charge_pool with day-recharge (Goat of Traveling pattern)","justification":"Goat of Traveling uses a 24-charge pool where each hour of use costs 1 charge and the pool recharges after 7 days when empty. This is neither use_count (fixed cap + rest reset) nor spell_slot. Needs a charge resource with duration-based consumption and day-count recharge.","evidence":"It has 24 charges, and each hour or portion thereof it spends in goat form costs 1 charge. When it runs out of charges, it reverts to a figurine and can't be used again until 7 days have passed, when it regains all expended charges."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"multi-variant item (one item slug, several named sub-configurations)","justification":"The Figurine of Wondrous Power is a single item category with nine distinct named variants (Bronze Griffon, Ebony Fly, Golden Lions, Ivory Goats × 3, Marble Elephant, Obsidian Steed, Onyx Dog, Serpentine Owl, Silver Raven). No surface type models this one-to-many item/variant relationship.","evidence":"Bronze Griffon (Rare)... Ebony Fly (Rare)... Golden Lions (Rare)... Ivory Goats (Rare)... Obsidian Steed (Very Rare)... Onyx Dog (Rare)... Serpentine Owl (Rare)... Silver Raven (Uncommon)."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"create_companion mechanics subgraph","justification":"The core effect is summoning a named creature that acts as a friendly companion with initiative placement, obeys commands, and reverts on 0 HP or dismissal. The v4 atom create_companion exists but there is no surface mechanics shape that expresses: throw-to-point activation, creature-kind binding, duration-to-revert lifecycle, or companion command semantics.","evidence":"The creature is Friendly to you and your allies. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"probabilistic_override (Obsidian Steed 10% disobedience)","justification":"The Obsidian Steed has a 10% per-use chance to ignore all commands including revert. This is not representable by any existing resolution atom (attack_roll, save_gate, ability_check). It requires a probability-weighted override that bypasses the normal command chain.","evidence":"The figurine has a 10 percent chance each time you use it to ignore your orders, including a command to revert to figurine form."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_figurine_of_wondrous_power.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
