../../results-srd/magic_item_periapt_of_proof_against_poison/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_periapt_of_proof_against_poison","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord + passive_while_attuned family","justification":"UnitRecord has no magic_item variant. The item's mechanic is a passive always-on effect while worn and attuned — no activation, no cost, no reset. No existing mechanics family (activation, ongoing_effect, on_hit_trigger, etc.) honestly represents this shape. A new top-level record kind and a new mechanics family are both required.","evidence":"While you wear it, you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition and Poison damage."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_immunity","justification":"v4 has grant_resistance (halved damage) but not grant_immunity (no damage/effect). These are mechanically distinct in SRD 5.2.1 — immunity fully negates while resistance halves. A separate atom is required to avoid a dishonest encoding that collapses the two.","evidence":"you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition and Poison damage"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_condition_immunity","justification":"v4 has apply_condition and remove_condition but no atom for granting permanent immunity to a condition. Condition immunity is mechanically distinct from resistance (which applies only to damage) and from remove_condition (which is a one-time effect).","evidence":"you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"attunement requirement on item record","justification":"The item requires attunement. v4 has attunement_slot as a resource atom and attune as a procedure atom, but the surface has no field on a hypothetical MagicItemRecord to express requires_attunement as a gate. This is a structural surface gap, not just