tureMechanics. No honest mapping exists without promoting a class feature to a mastery record, which misrepresents provenance.","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"choose_one_of DamageType at activation time","justification":"Primal Strike's 1d8 elemental damage type is chosen by the player at the moment of the hit, from the set {cold, fire, lightning, thunder}. DamageEffect.damageType is a single fixed DamageType with no 'choose_one_of' variant. A new surface shape is needed to express a runtime player choice among a closed set of damage types.","evidence":"you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (choose when you hit)"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"MasteryTrigger variant: weapon_or_wild_shape_beast_attack","justification":"Primal Strike fires on 'a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape.' The existing MasteryTrigger variants only cover weapon_hit and weapon_hit_melee_only. Wild Shape Beast-form natural attacks are not weapon attacks and require a new trigger category.","evidence":"when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or a Beast form's attack in Wild Shape"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/druid_elemental_fury_l7.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
