../../results-srd/cleric_blessed_strikes_l7/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"cleric_blessed_strikes_l7","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"choose_one_of","justification":"Blessed Strikes presents two mutually exclusive mechanical options; the player picks one permanently. No ClassFeatureMechanics family represents a 'choose one alternative' structure. The single activation family encodes exactly one effect, not a disjunction of options.","evidence":"You gain one of the following options of your choice (if you get either option from a Cleric subclass in an older book, use only the option you choose for this feature)."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"damage_on_hit_rider (ClassFeatureEffect)","justification":"Divine Strike adds extra damage on a weapon hit, once per turn. ClassFeatureEffect only contains grant_extra_action and heal_hp. The on_hit_trigger family exists only in MasteryMechanics. A class feature that grants a per-turn on-hit damage rider cannot be expressed without adding a new ClassFeatureEffect variant (or extending ClassFeatureMechanics with an on_hit_trigger family).","evidence":"Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice)."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"player_choice_damage_type","justification":"Divine Strike lets the player choose Necrotic or Radiant at the moment of the hit. DamageType is a single closed string; there is no 'one of [type_a, type_b] chosen at activation' variant. This is distinct from a fixed type.","evidence":"...the target to take an extra 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice)."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"add_ability_mod_to_damage","justification":"Potent Spellcasting adds the caster's Wisdom modifier (an ability score) to the damage dealt by cantrips. No v4 atom models this. modify_roll_numeric covers roll bonuses (Bless, Bane). scale_numeric_bonus covers level-scaled flat bonuses. None covers 'flat damage bonus equal to a specific ability modifier applied per-cantrip-damage-instance'.","evidence":"Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Cleric cantrip."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/cleric_blessed_strikes_l7.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0.001}
