../../results-srd/magic_item_dancing_sword/verdict.json:1:{"unit_slug":"magic_item_dancing_sword","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":-1,"tracer_exit":-1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"MagicItemRecord","justification":"No magic_item kind exists in UnitRecord. The current union is SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. Magic items need a new top-level record type (UnitMetadata & { kind: 'magic_item'; requiresAttunement: boolean; mechanics: MagicItemMechanics }) before any encoding can proceed.","evidence":"Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"attack_proxy_family","justification":"The Dancing Sword creates an autonomous weapon proxy that flies, repositions, and attacks independently using the wielder's attack roll and ability modifier. It tracks a 4-attack budget before auto-returning. No existing mechanics family (ongoing_effect, activation, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger, on_hit_trigger) can honestly represent: (a) an autonomous proxy making independent attacks, (b) a per-use countdown driving a forced lifecycle transition (return-to-hand), (c) repeatable Bonus-Action reposition+attack on subsequent turns. The v4 taxonomy has attack_proxy attachment and create_attack_proxy effect atoms, but no family wires them into a coherent subgraph.","evidence":"the weapon begins to hover, flies up to 30 feet, and attacks one creature of your choice within 5 feet of itself. The weapon uses your attack roll and adds your ability modifier to damage rolls. [...] After the hovering weapon attacks for the fourth time, it flies back to you"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"attune procedure in surface types","justification":"Attunement is a prerequisite for this item and is listed as a v4 atom ('attune') in TAXONOMY_atoms_graph.md, but there is no attunement_slot resource, no attune procedure, and no attunement_slot cap in types.ts. Any honest MagicItemRecord encoding needs attunement modeled at the surface.","evidence":"Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["no content/magic_item_dancing_sword.json authored; accepted self-report-only widening path"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":0}
